  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Bai Ning Bing first names Poison Vow Gu while traveling toward Shang clan city, planning to buy one there to bind Fang Yuan over the Yang Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          233
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_bai_ning_bing",
          "loc_shang_clan_city",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "gu_yang_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Once already in Shang clan city, she thinks again of forcing an unbreakable agreement with it.",
        "chapters": [
          260
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The first fully shown use is when Shang Ya Zi and Fang Yuan swear their recipe sale on it.",
        "chapters": [
          268
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_shang_ya_zi"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Bai Ning Bing refuses a casual promise and demands Poison Vow Gu for their split of gains and help with cultivation. They buy one in the third inner city; she refines it herself in about fifteen minutes so Fang Yuan cannot tamper, then they use it at Nan Qiu garden.",
        "chapters": [
          272
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "bai-ning-bings-alliance-vow",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_nan_qiu_garden"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan later removes only his own side of the vows with a temporary Eating One’s Words Gu, leaving Shang Ya Zi and Bai Ning Bing still bound. From previous-life knowledge he also names the later replacement chain: black and white paper Gu replaces Poison Vow Gu and cannot be broken by Eating One’s Words Gu, then distorting black and white Gu overrules that paper Gu. Poison Vow Gu, Eating One’s Words Gu, black and white paper Gu, and distorting black and white Gu form one stretch of the longer struggle between agreements and breaking them.",
        "chapters": [
          278
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "bai-ning-bings-alliance-vow",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "He also produces a Poison Vow Gu when Li Ran asks how to trust him.",
        "chapters": [
          285
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "bai-ning-bings-alliance-vow",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_li_ran"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Mountain pledge Gu and sea oath Gu worked like Poison Vow Gu, but Poison Vow Gu is an expenditure Gu while those two Immortal Gu can be used repeatedly.",
        "chapters": [
          384
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mountain-pledge-and-sea-oath",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_mountain_pledge_gu",
          "gu_sea_oath_gu",
          "sys_immortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Chou Jiu later calls Poison Vow Gu mountain pledge and sea oath Gu’s replacement when he explains how Doctor Su Shou escaped a vow: she lacks the ability to negate it, so she lets the vow kill her, then revives herself after the host-bound strength vanishes.",
        "chapters": [
          401
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mountain-pledge-and-sea-oath",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_chou_jiu",
          "char_doctor_su_shou"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Doctor Su Shou cannot dispel a poison vow outright. She instead lets the vow kill the bound Gu Master, clearing the poison, then revives that person; Bai Ning Bing uses that method to escape the bond with Fang Yuan.",
        "chapters": [
          396
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mountain-pledge-and-sea-oath",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "When Hei Lou Lan’s alliance seals its covenant, the leaders, including Fang Yuan, use Poison Vow Gu; the narration calls it the foundation of building mutual trust.",
        "chapters": [
          500
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mountain-pledge-and-sea-oath",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_hei_lou_lan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Later, when Eighty-Eight True Yang Building opens outward, Hei Pei requires entrants to use Poison Vow Gu and agree to give fifty percent of gains to Hei tribe.",
        "chapters": [
          562
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mountain-pledge-and-sea-oath",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
          "char_hei_pei",
          "fac_hei_tribe"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
